      "number_system": {
        "title": "Numbers",
        "principles": [
          "Numbers are organized through octaves.",
          "If the lower octave forms a circle, the higher octave forms a square. The square is the best representation because it tries to resolve limits within a repeated area.",
          "Circle, from outside, looks square; square, from outside, looks circle.",
          "In LaeChing, in trigrams 8, square and circle come in one; in hexagrams 64, in another. Because the higher octave of 8 must match the lower of 64, they have to be reverse-directional.",
          "For this reason, sometimes the naming of the first and second groups of four could be switched to show relative positioning in curvature layers and levels.",
          "On the first hyperoctave, circle seems larger; on the second, square seems larger. Even orientation is color-coding things."
        ],
        "groups": [
